# (#126) A numeric PARAMETER used as a for BINDER inside an OBSERVED
# function, where the parameter is named by no observer read.
#
# THE POINT: this shape was SILENTLY WRONG before the per-name gate, and
# the fixture is the discriminator for the binder arms (invariant 22 -- the
# first per-name binder fixture put its binder on the terminal env arm and
# stayed green with all three binder conversions reverted). Measured on the
# base compiler: post-loop `x` read 9 -- the last ITERABLE element, left in
# the env by the terminal env arm -- where the VM's parameter binding holds
# 4 and then 2:
#
#   f of 4.0   VM ["moving", 4, 25]    AOT ["moving", 9, 25]
#   f of 2.0   VM ["moving", 2, 24.5]  AOT ["moving", 9, 24.5]
#   both rc 0, no diagnostic
#
# The g_observed guard on the numeric-parameter binder arm was load-bearing
# for a NAMED parameter (an observed function routes those through the env,
# so a C-var write there is a dead store) and over-broad for every other
# one; per-name it fires exactly where the parameter really is a C double.
define f(x) as:
    local w is x
    w is w * 0.5
    w is w * 0.5
    for x in [7.0, 8.0, 9.0]:
        w is w + x
    return [report of w, x, w]
print of (f of 4.0)
print of (f of 2.0)
